; 44-sort.kurt

; Kurt's sorts are kinds of objects -- of terms: `any` (every object) is in every file, and a theory
; declares its own below `any` (they may form a DAG). Statements (`prop`, lesson 01) are no sort and
; no object: they are what is proved. The rules in short (the tutorial's
; lesson 29 shows them at work; doc/kurt-soundness.md §10 why they are sound):
;   - every symbol has a sort; without one it is `any`, and a constant gets its sort at its first
;     sorted use -- which is final;
;   - a value fits a place of its own sort or of a bigger one;
;   - `∀ x` and `∃ x` range over the sort of `x`; a fact gives no sort;
;   - a rule for every sort writes its bound variables `$$x`.

sort nat, vec

; A sort name becomes a declaration keyword parallel to `prop`. Position 0 is
; the result; positions 1, 2, ... are arguments. A position left out takes every
; value (it is `any`).

nat zero
nat plus 0 1 2
vec scale 0 2
nat scale 1

arity plus 2, scale 2

; A sort property does not choose `const` or `var`.

var n, v
nat n
vec v

; Subsorts: a chain `sort big small` declares `small ⊂ big` -- a `small` fits where a `big` is
; required (objects.kurt has `sort set real`: a number is a set).

sort nat pos
pos one

; `any` declares a symbol of all objects: it fits only where `any` (or no sort) is required, and no
; use changes it.

any thing

; A sort declaration comes before the symbol's first use, and its first sorted use decides a sort
; for good: to use a constant as a smaller sort, declare that first.

const g
arity g 1
pos g 1                               ; `g` takes a `pos`
const k
use plus k k = k                      ; `k` is a `nat` from here on
expect "TypeError" "but here it is used as `pos`"
    use g k = g k                     ; a smaller sort later: declare `pos k` before the first use

; `default SORT` at the top of a file gives every new symbol without a sort that sort (a file about
; numbers says `default real`); `default any` is the same as none.

; `sort`, and each individual sort name, list their declarations.

sort
nat
